},"identifiers":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df/identifiers"},"mappedCollections":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df/mappedCollections"},"owningCollection":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df/owningCollection"},"relationships":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df/relationships"},"version":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df/version"},"templateItemOf":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df/templateItemOf"},"thumbnail":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df/thumbnail"},"self":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df"}},"_name":"Market equilibrium without profit maximization: a process of demand discovery from a smithian perspective","id":"53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df","uuid":"53cbfd20-cee4-45f0-b3a2-8092fed9b3df","type":"item","metadata":{"dc.creator":[{"uuid":"5bffd973-0eb9-4cc5-a84c-39b8b590f01b","language":null,"value":"Michele Bee","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"2b92245b-edee-444b-b882-fc36157377b6","language":null,"value":"Juan Pablo Gama","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"e954ef41-b2c0-41da-9f87-abc22536acfb","language":null,"value":"Italo Parrilli","place":2,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.accessioned":[{"uuid":"eacf2172-3a4b-48b5-80af-15bb943d4fd2","language":null,"value":"2026-10-29T12:57:35Z","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.issued":[{"uuid":"78bc5c6a-4d44-4538-8471-cdf79de93a72","language":null,"value":"2026","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.identifier.uri":[{"uuid":"cbe2fd07-170b-40b5-8bcd-e4125bda9d8e","language":null,"value":"https://hdl.handle.net/1843/6049","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.language":[{"uuid":"de97c085-6b84-427b-8bba-e6b8c5b5528b","language":null,"value":"eng","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.publisher":[{"uuid":"6c93ec3f-b01c-4773-af79-06f11ad3b329","language":null,"value":"Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.relation.ispartof":[{"uuid":"f4d0e5e2-8ec6-462b-986b-8e0057ece66d","language":null,"value":"Seminário de Diamantina","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.rights":[{"uuid":"74c9f048-9e82-4180-9836-8208f8a7f115","language":null,"value":"Acesso aberto","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.subject":[{"uuid":"445dd5e7-b674-4758-87bb-e43e3cb3619c","language":null,"value":"Economia","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.subject.other":[{"uuid":"aef04ff1-8324-4f13-bc22-1644b63a1dd6","language":null,"value":"Natural price","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"506abe47-6318-4755-a8b1-d886507a19a8","language":null,"value":"Imperfect competition","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"b2a80b20-469f-4b69-be5a-0080aa611926","language":null,"value":"Smithian theory of market price convergence","place":2,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"8cd8f837-a082-4854-a427-9817869ff586","language":null,"value":"RIvalry","place":3,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.title":[{"uuid":"c58b3fc9-e695-44b1-bdd3-c784f624b02e","language":null,"value":"Market equilibrium without profit maximization: a process of demand discovery from a smithian perspective","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.type":[{"uuid":"5b2daa6e-dc68-4894-af88-7e561ec1d01a","language":null,"value":"Artigo de evento","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.citation.issue":[{"uuid":"3b9a7b64-ef29-42e9-8ec3-8b80eca51cda","language":null,"value":"21","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.description.resumo":[{"uuid":"9f737ecd-e9be-43e6-8226-8e72541ecd1c","language":null,"value":"This paper presents a competitive market model where firms do not maximize profits, do not know the demand curve, and do not behave as price takers. Market equilibrium is achieved by producers whose aim is to satisfy as far as possible the demand of consumers willing to pay a price that properly remunerates costs, i.e., the natural price (or reserve price). Agents estimate demand through a market learning process based on linear interpolation and Bayesian updating, without relying on profit maximization and perfect information assumptions. Building on Adam Smith’s theory of convergence of the market price to the natural price, in a repeated multi-period game, producers set their supply to meet the entire demand at the reserve price. Rivalry-driven price deviations are the only information firms use to update beliefs. But the stronger this competition is, the slower the discovery process. Treating natural price and effectual demand as an Aspiration-Based Competitive Equilibrium (ABCE) not only sheds new light on the description of the market in The Wealth of Nations, but also help us to explain market dynamics, without necessarily assuming maximizing behavior. This paper describes the convergence process absent in neoclassical theory, showing that competition can play a different role in price formation than assumed in that theory.","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.publisher.country":[{"uuid":"7e657a28-3e35-4e42-bca7-19a8480e5998","language":null,"value":"Brasil","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.publisher.department":[{"uuid":"383c0461-eb89-4635-9b44-4d881dd67ace","language":null,"value":"FCE - DEPARTAMENTO DE CIÊNCIAS ECONÔMICAS","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.publisher.initials":[{"uuid":"bf2c2ec6-c523-48e4-8611-9cc86b980604","language":null,"value":"UFMG","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.subject.cnpq":[{"uuid":"86e1044b-8bdf-4723-92c4-697c5eea1cd1","language":null,"value":"CIENCIAS SOCIAIS APLICADAS","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}]}},"timeCompleted":1793292501288,"msToLive":900000,"requestUUIDs":["client/da560174-8c32-4626-91c7-182d07b58419"],"dependentRequestUUIDs":[],"isDirty":false,"patches":[],"alternativeLinks":[]},"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/thumbnail":{"data":null,"timeCompleted":1793292501288,"msToLive":900000,"requestUUIDs":["client/da560174-8c32-4626-91c7-182d07b58419"],"dependentRequestUUIDs":["client/da560174-8c32-4626-91c7-182d07b58419"],"isDirty":false,"patches":[],"alternativeLinks":["https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/thumbnail"]},"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182":{"data":{"handle":"1843/6048","lastModified":"2026-10-29T12:38:48.382Z","isArchived":true,"isDiscoverable":true,"isWithdrawn":false,"_links":{"accessStatus":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/accessStatus"},"bundles":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/bundles"},"identifiers":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/identifiers"},"mappedCollections":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/mappedCollections"},"owningCollection":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/owningCollection"},"relationships":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/relationships"},"version":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/version"},"templateItemOf":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/templateItemOf"},"thumbnail":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182/thumbnail"},"self":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182"}},"_name":"Growth arrested live-attenuated Leishmania infantum KHARON1 null mutants display cytokinesis defect and protective immunity in mice","id":"1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182","uuid":"1be39b67-5a2b-4a98-b16e-d17cf08d0182","type":"item","metadata":{"dc.creator":[{"uuid":"93c243a8-ed48-4650-a188-ba96d54bc75d","language":null,"value":"Ana Maria Murta Santi","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"773fcab9-44fe-4823-a250-618f1aa114c9","language":null,"value":"Juliane Sousa Lanza","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"c4ae552c-c0a2-48a1-94ab-9ef53231703a","language":null,"value":"Luiza Guimarães Tunes","place":2,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"3f790794-5a2d-41ee-8a7a-bcc500bc012b","language":null,"value":"Jacqueline Araújo Fiuza","place":3,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"8aa13fc7-660d-423c-ab3c-8eeab7f17d8b","language":null,"value":"Gaétan Roy","place":4,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"7b2b4438-5f5e-4afc-83bb-ade357ca7da4","language":null,"value":"Alessandra da Silva Orfanó","place":5,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"16051279-dfef-45c1-acd3-7cc5dee8fa57","language":null,"value":"Andréa Teixeira de Carvalho","place":6,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"c7314d3c-e216-4e8b-9a33-ddfbc1470d6f","language":null,"value":"Frederic Jean Georges Frezard","place":7,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"9916da72-7aa5-446a-93a2-bfce78b562a2","language":null,"value":"André Luís Branco de Barros","place":8,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"45dd14f2-626c-4ca1-b864-5b7591d84abc","language":null,"value":"Silvane Maria Fonseca Murta","place":9,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"841ed8ac-af44-47b9-9bab-ceeae4e1c57f","language":null,"value":"Rubens Lima do Monte Neto","place":10,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.accessioned":[{"uuid":"fc48a470-71b8-4945-848b-74118b1f8918","language":null,"value":"2026-10-29T12:38:48Z","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.date.issued":[{"uuid":"c788a2c7-b41f-4682-997c-77614bb99e31","language":null,"value":"2018","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.description.abstract":[{"uuid":"b684e83d-d1dd-4e9e-9b33-5c5fbc75661e","language":null,"value":"Não existe uma vacina segura e eficaz disponível contra a leishmaniose humana, e vacinas com patógenos vivos atenuados têm sido utilizadas como uma alternativa profilática contra a doença. Com o objetivo de obter um parasita Leishmania atenuado para fins vacinais, geramos mutantes nulos de L. infantum para o gene KHARON1 (KH1) (ΔLikh1). Esse gene foi previamente associado a defeitos no crescimento em L. mexicana. A linhagem ΔLikh1 foi obtida e confirmada por meio de PCR, qPCR e Southern blot. Também geramos uma linhagem com o gene KH1 complementado, por meio da introdução de cópias epissomais de KH1. Embora as formas promastigotas de ΔLikh1 tenham apresentado um padrão de crescimento semelhante ao da linhagem selvagem, elas diferem na morfologia, sem que isso afete a viabilidade do parasita. As formas amastigotas de L. infantum deficientes em KH1 não conseguiram manter uma infecção experimental em macrófagos, resultando na formação de células multinucleadas - um fenômeno confirmado pelo fenótipo de atenuação in vivo. A análise do ciclo celular das amastigotas ΔLikh1 revelou células com interrupção na fase G2/M. Camundongos imunizados com ΔLikh1 apresentaram uma carga parasitária reduzida após o desafio com L. infantum virulento, em comparação com camundongos não imunizados. Esse efeito esteve associado a níveis séricos mais elevados de IgG específica contra antígenos solúveis de L. infantum (Li SLA) e a uma maior produção de IL-17. Portanto, os parasitas ΔLikh1 apresentam um fenótipo atenuado - porém ainda capaz de infectar - decorrente de um defeito na citocinese; ao mesmo tempo, induzem imunidade contra a leishmaniose visceral em modelos murinos, tornando-se, assim, candidatos para o desenvolvimento de uma vacina contra a leishmaniose.","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.description.sponsorship":[{"uuid":"554e2fa6-6742-4629-9176-c6d2f2d3030b","language":null,"value":"CNPq - Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Científico e Tecnológico","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"95b9d41e-0e1d-47d7-85b4-1c935519f047","language":null,"value":"CAPES - Coordenação de Aperfeiçoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.identifier.doi":[{"uuid":"afce7270-6078-49ed-8135-da6a7e831ffe","language":null,"value":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-018-30076-7","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.identifier.issn":[{"uuid":"bb361c07-1e84-42ee-87a5-2f7e414495a5","language":null,"value":"2045-2322","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.identifier.uri":[{"uuid":"e02e95fb-73f6-47b1-b3d1-02860d1752f1","language":null,"value":"https://hdl.handle.net/1843/6048","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.language":[{"uuid":"54f484ca-6388-4b82-9c52-a405ee830854","language":"pt_BR","value":"Inglês","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.publisher":[{"uuid":"1d58b031-5e3b-40f7-b32e-cfc7f736d478","language":null,"value":"Universidade Federal de Minas Gerais","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.relation.ispartof":[{"uuid":"c704e388-7e47-40ea-88b6-8be166d7747a","language":null,"value":"Scientific Reports","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.rights":[{"uuid":"55cdb478-22f8-4345-afd6-c7e4d7fe8a53","language":null,"value":"Acesso aberto","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.subject":[{"uuid":"cb67f01f-bf97-416d-9c13-326b28535555","language":null,"value":"Citocinese","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"367b93d8-b028-44a4-9ea6-b5afc46d1e60","language":null,"value":"Genômica","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"9f14a923-7ed5-4421-895b-1f958b947173","language":null,"value":"Doenças parasitárias","place":2,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"8f202bc6-6be3-4a36-85f0-df1ce960fd62","language":null,"value":"Parasitologia","place":3,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"e3194285-c83d-4dbf-aca8-922a71441230","language":null,"value":"Leishmaniose","place":4,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"b6b35071-722a-4195-b712-d9d672e7d396","language":null,"value":"Leishmania infantum","place":5,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"ac878e93-2f53-4115-a3c2-54866e451a09","language":null,"value":"Imunidade","place":6,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"add1486f-4569-4147-98ad-2807ce6f8eaa","language":null,"value":"Vacinas","place":7,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.subject.other":[{"uuid":"f816f4c2-1f95-4efb-adcd-68e89e7cfa68","language":null,"value":"Cytokinesis","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"6b5fe8a6-cb67-47b9-a80a-cee008ff2b43","language":null,"value":"Functional genomics","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"eb33d6f3-2fab-4dbb-b43e-c664b6484293","language":null,"value":"Parasitic infection","place":2,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"1be4da96-b3b6-4d36-89b6-37b38d576d70","language":null,"value":"Parasitology","place":3,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"00aeebfd-32de-474e-9622-31dccc9faa34","language":null,"value":"Leishmaniasis epidemiology","place":4,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"838993e3-8b66-4e7a-9c3f-ad8da7013f97","language":null,"value":"Immune responses","place":5,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.title":[{"uuid":"398d4c90-7951-4a93-8557-90d4c95e14cb","language":null,"value":"Growth arrested live-attenuated Leishmania infantum KHARON1 null mutants display cytokinesis defect and protective immunity in mice","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"dc.type":[{"uuid":"fa475ea0-caec-4594-b2c5-3c108ef62950","language":null,"value":"Artigo de periódico","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.citation.epage":[{"uuid":"602ece9f-122a-4032-8a92-a1b4f9b52198","language":null,"value":"15","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.citation.issue":[{"uuid":"9c1cffed-6152-43a7-ae85-29c7e7e5ca3f","language":null,"value":"1","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.citation.spage":[{"uuid":"ccc05fb8-ca6e-4b9c-b809-154dc85393be","language":null,"value":"1","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.citation.volume":[{"uuid":"98c6a2e6-29a0-41db-8af7-d814e422bbaf","language":null,"value":"8","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.description.resumo":[{"uuid":"fc965155-8b7f-4bba-9ec3-7d6e1952191c","language":null,"value":"There is no safe and efficacious vaccine against human leishmaniasis available and live attenuated vaccines have been used as a prophylactic alternative against the disease. In order to obtain an attenuated Leishmania parasite for vaccine purposes, we generated L. infantum KHARON1 (KH1) null mutants (ΔLikh1). This gene was previously associated with growth defects in L. mexicana. ΔLikh1 was obtained and confirmed by PCR, qPCR and Southern blot. We also generate a KH1 complemented line with the introduction of episomal copies of KH1. Although ΔLikh1 promastigote forms exhibited a growth pattern similar to the wild-type line, they differ in morphology without affecting parasite viability. L. infantum KH1-deficient amastigotes were unable to sustain experimental infection in macrophages, forming multinucleate cells which was confirmed by in vivo attenuation phenotype. The cell cycle analysis of ΔLikh1 amastigotes showed arrested cells at G2/M phase. ΔLikh1-immunized mice presented reduced parasite burden upon challenging with virulent L. infantum, when compared to naïve mice. An effect associated with increased Li SLA-specific IgG serum levels and IL-17 production. Thus, ΔLikh1 parasites present an infective-attenuated phenotype due to a cytokinesis defect, whereas it induces immunity against visceral leishmaniasis in mouse model, being a candidate for antileishmanial vaccine purposes.","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.publisher.country":[{"uuid":"ff5945fc-9402-4b15-990f-9bcc141efb32","language":null,"value":"Brasil","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.publisher.department":[{"uuid":"609f7d29-c806-4448-991d-348aca661178","language":null,"value":"FAR - DEPARTAMENTO DE ANÁLISES CLÍNICAS E TOXICOLÓGICAS","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1},{"uuid":"86c67b5d-b28a-4643-aa9a-c312c6ed0233","language":null,"value":"ICB - DEPARTAMENTO DE FISIOLOGIA E BIOFÍSICA","place":1,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.publisher.initials":[{"uuid":"a1fdd9e1-c7f4-45d0-adab-59e0a0fefb96","language":null,"value":"UFMG","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.subject.cnpq":[{"uuid":"d23e6772-c8de-40b8-8e2a-946478f0fcfc","language":null,"value":"CIENCIAS DA SAUDE","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}],"local.url.externa":[{"uuid":"aad5a906-6d9d-45e8-87a9-2ce306136811","language":null,"value":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41598-018-30076-7#citeas","place":0,"authority":null,"confidence":-1}]}},"timeCompleted":1793292501288,"msToLive":900000,"requestUUIDs":["client/da560174-8c32-4626-91c7-182d07b58419"],"dependentRequestUUIDs":[],"isDirty":false,"patches":[],"alternativeLinks":[]},"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/discover/search/objects?dsoType=ITEM&sort=dc.date.accessioned,DESC&size=5":{"data":{"type":{"value":"discovery-objects"},"page":[{"type":{"value":"searchresult"},"hitHighlights":{},"_links":{"indexableObject":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/b5310d06-b72f-464e-951a-36515b990ffd"}}},{"type":{"value":"searchresult"},"hitHighlights":{},"_links":{"indexableObject":{"href":"https://repositorio.ufmg.br/server/api/core/items/404680c0-dec0-4980-998a-9d47c3df2a0e"}}},{"type":{"value":